# Directory Structure Rules

## Project Structure

- The project is organized into `frontend` and `backend` directories at the root level
- Do not create nested folders with the same name (e.g., do not create `backend/backend` or `frontend/frontend`)
- When running commands, be careful with directory paths to avoid creating unintended nested directories

## Backend Structure

- Source code is in the `src` directory
- Tests are in the `src/__tests__` directory
- Configuration files should be at the root of the backend directory

## Command Execution

- When executing commands, always check your current working directory
- Use relative paths when appropriate
- When using `cd` commands, verify the path is correct before executing 